-- title:
--   Cyclic covers of xy=πⁿ unramified in codimension one are Kummer
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, complete with respect to its maximal-ideal adic topology, let $\pi$ be an irreducible element of $W$, and let $n$ be a positive natural number which is invertible in $W$ and such that $W$ contains a primitive $n$-th root of unity. Write $R_0 =$ `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ (1 * n))` for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi^{1\cdot n}$ (the exponent appearing literally as $1\cdot n$, the thickness-one case). Let $K_0$ be a field equipped with an $R_0$-algebra structure making it a fraction field of $R_0$, and let $F$ be a field which is an algebra over both $K_0$ and $R_0$ in a compatible way (scalar tower), finite and Galois over $K_0$ with cyclic Galois group $F \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K_0]} F$ and $[F:K_0] = n$. Let $B$ be the integral closure of $R_0$ in $F$, assumed to be a local ring, and assume: (i) for every prime ideal $Q$ of $B$ whose contraction along $R_0 \to B$ has height $1$, the algebra $B$ is unramified over $R_0$ at $Q$; (ii) every $b \in B$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $B$ to the image in $B$ of the class of a constant power series $C(w)$ with $w \in W$. Then there exist a unit $u$ of $R_0$ and an element $\theta \in F$ with $\theta^n$ equal to the image in $F$ of $u \cdot U(\pi^{1\cdot n})$, where $U(\pi^{1\cdot n})$ is the distinguished branch element of $R_0$, and with $K_0(\theta) = F$, i.e. the intermediate field generated over $K_0$ by $\theta$ is all of $F$.
--
--   This is the Kummer-generator step (in the spirit of Abhyankar's lemma and tame Kummer theory) for degree-$n$ cyclic covers of the local crossing model $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi^{n})$: a cyclic cover which is unramified over all height-one primes and has rational residue data at the closed point is generated by an $n$-th root of a unit multiple of one branch coordinate. It is used by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel_of_isGalois_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel_of_isGalois_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue), where the integral closure is then identified with a crossing model of smaller thickness, in the analysis of the local structure of stable models of modular curves at supersingular points.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_pow_eq_unit_mul_U_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue_thicknessOne.lean

